  "unresolvedAiThreads": [
    {
      "threadId": "PRRT_kwDORKRjBc6cD_zt",
      "replyToCommentDatabaseId": 3852762741,
      "path": "VAA.EAPI.Microservices/VAA.EAPI.Microservices.Retail.Holidays/Application/RetrieveDocumentService.cs",
      "line": 233,
      "url": "https://github.com/VAAD1ST/eapi/pull/1742#discussion_r3852762741",
      "author": "copilot-pull-request-reviewer",
      "body": "`Holidays:DocumentDownloadTimeoutSeconds` is read directly into `CancelAfter`. If it is misconfigured to a negative or zero value, `CancelAfter(TimeSpan.FromSeconds(...))` can throw `ArgumentOutOfRangeException`, turning a configuration issue into a 500 and bypassing the controller’s controlled error mapping. Consider clamping to a safe minimum (or falling back to the default) before calling `CancelAfter`.",
      "decision": "valid",
      "resolutionComment": "Valid. ConfigReader accepts a configured non-positive integer, which was passed directly to CancellationTokenSource.CancelAfter. The download timeout is now clamped to a one-second minimum, with regression coverage for zero and negative configuration values."
    },
    {
      "threadId": "PRRT_kwDORKRjBc6cD_0l",
      "replyToCommentDatabaseId": 3852762809,
      "path": "VAA.EAPI.GraphQL/VAA.EAPI.GraphQL.Domain.Trips/Queries/HolidayQuery.cs",
      "line": 512,
      "url": "https://github.com/VAAD1ST/eapi/pull/1742#discussion_r3852762809",
      "author": "copilot-pull-request-reviewer",
      "body": "When the requested `documentId` does not match the token’s `document-id` claim, the resolver throws `new GraphQLException(string)` without a status code. This makes the client-visible error harder to handle consistently (vs the other controlled 400/404 paths in this resolver). Return a controlled BadRequest GraphQL error with an explicit 400 code instead.",
      "decision": "valid",
      "resolutionComment": "Valid. The document-ID mismatch branch used the GraphQLException string constructor while adjacent validation paths returned explicit client-facing codes. It now builds a controlled GraphQL error with code 400, covered by a focused mismatch test."
    }
  ],
